---
/** Privacy Policy & Terms page. Ported from react/pages/Legal.tsx. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BackLink from "../components/BackLink.astro";
import {
  LEGAL_NOTICE,
  formatLegalDate,
  legalNoticeEffectiveDate,
} from "../../../src/react/lib/legal-notice";

// The same constant drives the "terms changed" toast, so the date the page
// prints and the date the toast announces cannot disagree.
const published = formatLegalDate(LEGAL_NOTICE.version);
const effective = formatLegalDate(legalNoticeEffectiveDate(LEGAL_NOTICE));
---

<Base title="GlideComp - Privacy Policy & Terms">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground py-6 px-page-safe">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <BackLink href="/" />
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold flex items-center gap-3">
          <img src="/icon.svg" alt="GlideComp logo" class="w-8 h-8" />
          Privacy Policy &amp; Terms
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">Last updated: {published}</p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">
          The changes of {published} (Terms sections 5, 7 and 12) take effect on {effective}.
        </p>
      </header>

      {/* Table of Contents */}
      <nav class="mb-10 p-4 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground mb-2">
          Contents
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>
            <a href="#privacy-policy" class="hover:underline">
              Privacy Policy
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="#terms" class="hover:underline">
              Terms and Conditions
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      {/* Privacy Policy */}
      <section id="privacy-policy" class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Privacy Policy</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">1. Who We Are</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              GlideComp is a free, non-commercial service for scoring and analysing hang gliding and paragliding competitions, run by Tushar Pokle. For anything about your data — seeing it, correcting it, deleting it, or making a complaint — email <a href="mailto:tushar.pokle@gmail.com" class="underline hover:text-foreground">tushar.pokle@gmail.com</a>. Please don&rsquo;t use GitHub issues for this: they are public.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">2. What We Collect</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
              <li><strong>Your account.</strong> If you sign in with Google: your name, email address and profile picture. We don&rsquo;t access any other Google account data. If you sign in with an emailed code: your email address.</li>
              <li><strong>Sign-in sessions.</strong> Your IP address and browser type, kept with your session to keep you signed in and to protect against abuse.</li>
              <li><strong>Competition registrations.</strong> Your name, email address, class, glider, team, pilot ID numbers (such as CIVL, FAI, SAFA, USHPA, BHPA, DHV or FFVL), world ranking points and a driver contact. <strong>An organiser can enter these for you, even if you don&rsquo;t have a GlideComp account.</strong></li>
              <li><strong>Track logs (IGC files).</strong> Your flight&rsquo;s GPS positions, altitudes and times, and the pilot and glider details your flight instrument writes into the file.</li>
              <li><strong>What organisers create.</strong> Competitions, tasks, waypoints, penalties, pilot status (such as absent or landed) and weather notes.</li>
              <li><strong>Your own library.</strong> Tracks, tasks and notes you save to your account.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">3. What Is Public</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Competition results are public so that anyone can check them. For every competition except private test competitions, anyone — including search engines — can see pilot names and competition details (including glider and pilot ID numbers), track logs, scores and flight analysis, and the competition&rsquo;s activity log, which records who changed what.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
              Pilot email addresses and driver contacts are visible only to that competition&rsquo;s organisers. When a track is submitted for you, we email you the organisers&rsquo; names and email addresses so you can contact them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">4. Why We Use Your Data</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
              <li>To provide the service you use: your account, your uploads, and the competitions you run or fly in.</li>
              <li>To publish fair, checkable competition results — a legitimate interest shared by pilots and organisers.</li>
              <li>To email you every time a track is submitted for you, so a wrong or false submission can&rsquo;t go unnoticed.</li>
              <li>To keep the service secure and prevent abuse.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
              We don&rsquo;t sell your data, show advertising, use analytics or tracking, or send marketing email. The only emails we send are sign-in codes and track submission notices.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">5. Services We Use</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
              <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, database, file storage and sending email. Subject to
                <a
                  href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="underline hover:text-foreground"
                >Cloudflare&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a></li>
              <li><strong>Google</strong> — sign-in, if you choose it. Subject to
                <a
                  href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="underline hover:text-foreground"
                >Google&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a></li>
              <li><strong>Mapbox</strong> — maps, terrain heights and place search. Mapbox&rsquo;s map library sends anonymous usage data to Mapbox. Subject to
                <a
                  href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/privacy"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="underline hover:text-foreground"
                >Mapbox&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a></li>
              <li><strong>Open-Meteo</strong> — weather for a task. We send only the task&rsquo;s location and date. Subject to
                <a
                  href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="underline hover:text-foreground"
                >Open-Meteo&rsquo;s Terms</a></li>
              <li><strong>FAI / CIVL</strong> — we read the world rankings the FAI publishes. We send them nothing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">6. Where Your Data Is Stored</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              On Cloudflare&rsquo;s global network, which may be outside your country, including in the United States. Cloudflare&rsquo;s data processing terms include safeguards for international transfers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">7. Cookies &amp; Browser Storage</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We use only the cookies needed to keep you signed in — no advertising or analytics cookies. Your browser also keeps your preferences and cached data (localStorage and IndexedDB), which you can clear in your browser settings.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">8. How Long We Keep Data</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
              <li><strong>Your account and saved library:</strong> until you delete your account.</li>
              <li><strong>Sign-in sessions</strong> (with your IP address and browser type): a session ends after 60 days without use, and we delete it within a day of ending.</li>
              <li><strong>Sign-in codes:</strong> they expire after 10 minutes, and we delete them within a day.</li>
              <li><strong>IP addresses used to limit abuse</strong> (for example, of sign-in attempts and submissions made without an account): deleted within two days.</li>
              <li><strong>Competition data</strong> (registrations, tracks, scores and the activity log): kept as the published record of the competition, unless its organiser deletes the competition or we remove it on request (see section 9).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">9. Deleting Your Account</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              You can delete your account from your dashboard. This removes your account, profile, sessions and preferences, your saved tracks, tasks and notes, and your API keys, and revokes GlideComp&rsquo;s access to your Google account.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
              Competition records stay, but are no longer linked to your account: your registrations, the tracks you flew in competitions, your scores and activity log entries. They are part of each competition&rsquo;s published results, and removing them would change other pilots&rsquo; scores. If you want them removed or your name hidden, email us — we will work with the organiser and remove them unless there is a strong reason to keep them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">10. Your Rights</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              You can ask to see, correct or delete your data — including data an organiser entered about you — by emailing <a href="mailto:tushar.pokle@gmail.com" class="underline hover:text-foreground">tushar.pokle@gmail.com</a>. We will reply within 30 days. If you are not satisfied, you can complain to your local privacy regulator; in Australia, that is the
              <a
                  href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="underline hover:text-foreground"
                >OAIC</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">11. Security &amp; Breaches</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We take reasonable steps to protect your data, but no system is perfectly secure. If a breach puts your data at risk, we will tell you and the relevant regulator promptly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">12. Children</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              GlideComp is not directed at children under 13, and we don&rsquo;t knowingly collect their data. Junior pilots aged 13–17 may be registered by a competition organiser; a parent or guardian can ask us to remove a junior&rsquo;s data at <a href="mailto:tushar.pokle@gmail.com" class="underline hover:text-foreground">tushar.pokle@gmail.com</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">13. Changes</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We will tell you about material changes as described in the Terms (<a href="#terms-changes" class="underline hover:text-foreground">section 11</a>).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Terms and Conditions */}
      <section id="terms" class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Terms and Conditions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              By accessing or using GlideComp, you agree to be bound by these Terms and
              Conditions. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">2. Description of Service</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              GlideComp is a free tool for managing and scoring hanggliding and paragliding
              competitions. The service allows competition administrators to create competitions,
              define tasks, and manage pilot registrations. Pilots can upload IGC track files,
              which are analysed and scored automatically using the GAP formula. Task definitions
              and scoring results are publicly viewable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">3. User Accounts</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              You may create an account using Google sign-in or a code emailed to you. You are responsible for maintaining
              the security of your account. You may delete your account at any time.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">4. User Content</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              You retain ownership of any content you upload to GlideComp, including IGC track
              files and task definitions. By uploading content, you grant GlideComp a
              non-exclusive license to store, process, and display that content as necessary to
              provide the service. You may delete your content at any time.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">5. Organisers</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              If you run a competition on GlideComp, you are responsible for the pilot details you enter, such as names, email addresses, pilot ID numbers and driver contacts. Only enter details you are entitled to use to run the competition, keep them accurate, and correct or remove them when a pilot asks. Results, tracks and the activity log are public, so don&rsquo;t write anything in a penalty reason, weather note or other text field that you wouldn&rsquo;t say publicly about the pilot.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">6. Acceptable Use</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">You agree not to:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-1 mt-2">
              <li>Use the service for any unlawful purpose</li>
              <li>Attempt to interfere with the service's operation</li>
              <li>
                Reverse engineer or attempt to extract the source code (beyond what is publicly
                available on GitHub)
              </li>
              <li>Upload content you don&rsquo;t have the right to share, or enter false information about other people</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">7. Reporting Content</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              If you think something on GlideComp is wrong, unlawful or defamatory, or infringes your rights, email <a href="mailto:tushar.pokle@gmail.com" class="underline hover:text-foreground">tushar.pokle@gmail.com</a> with a link to it and a description of the problem. We will review it, and may edit, hide or remove it. We may also remove content, or suspend an account, that breaks these terms.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">8. Disclaimer of Warranties</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              GlideComp is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, either express or
              implied. We do not guarantee that the service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or
              that analysis results will be accurate. Flight analysis results should not be used
              as the sole basis for safety-critical decisions.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">9. Limitation of Liability</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              To the fullest extent permitted by law, GlideComp and its contributors shall not be
              liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from
              your use of the service.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">10. Open Source</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              GlideComp is open-source software. The source code is available on
              <a
                href="https://github.com/pokle/glidecomp"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="underline hover:text-foreground"
              >
                GitHub
              </a> and is subject to its own license terms.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div id="terms-changes">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">11. Changes to Terms</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We may update these terms. If a change materially affects you, we will show a notice on GlideComp at least 14 days before it takes effect. Minor changes, such as corrections and clarifications, take effect when we publish them. If you don&rsquo;t agree with a change, you can stop using GlideComp and delete your account. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page shows when these terms last changed.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">12. Governing Law</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia, and the courts of Victoria have jurisdiction. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law, including the Australian Consumer Law, that cannot be excluded.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">13. Contact</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:tushar.pokle@gmail.com" class="underline hover:text-foreground">tushar.pokle@gmail.com</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
